ros-rolling-off-highway-premium-radar (1.4.0-1resolute) resolute; urgency=high

  * Add extra validity check for locationsAn extra validation check was added to verify if the received location is a measured one or padding.
    
    Adapted test cases for new condition.
  * Remove io_context dependencyDue to build issues caused by another package, it was decided to remove the dependency to it in order to have a successful build on rolling.
  * Increase accepted timestamp delay for diagnostics to 150 msLarger delays can occur once PTP synchronization is active, so the
    previous 100 ms limit was too strict for off_highway_premium_radar
    and off_highway_premium_radar_sample default converters.
  * asio::ip::{address::from_string -> make_address} (#33)fix for asio 1.36
    
    from_string has been deprecated for at least 9 years (ref blame https://github.com/boostorg/asio/blame/b60e92b13ef68dfbb9af180d76eae41d22e19356/include/boost/asio/ip/address.hpp),
    and removed in https://github.com/boostorg/asio/commit/c0d1cfce7767599c4cf00df36f8017a1073339ae
    
    Applied to off_highway_premium_radar and off_highway_premium_radar_sample.
  * Contributors: Darius Man, David Mueller, Guilhem Saurel

 -- "Sarah Huber" <sarah.huber@de.bosch.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0000

